<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh 1996/97 sugar yield seen down 25 pct.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh 1996/97 sugar yield seen down 25 pct.</headline>
<dateline>DHAKA 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bangladesh's sugar production in 1996/97 (July-June) is expected to fall by 25 percent 135,000 tonnes, A.K. Munshi, Bangladesh Sugar and Food Industries Corp chairman said on Wednesday. &quot;Floods, disproportionate use of fertiliser and pesticides and growers apathy were responsible for lower production of sugar this year,&quot; Munshi told Reuters in an interview.  </p>
<p>Bangladesh had officially targetted sugar production of 215,000 tonnes for 1996/97, against an actual yield of 180,000 tonnes in 1995/96, Munshi said.</p>
</text>
